kosha phase

  -- the state of matter at everyday conditions (room temperature, normal pressure).
  -- not the physics of phase transitions — the everyday observation:
  -- water is liquid. ice is solid. air is gas. iron is solid. mercury is liquid.
  --
  -- three everyday phases:
  --
  --   solid    — holds its shape. resists deformation. can be stacked, lifted, thrown.
  --              examples: iron, wood, glass, stone, ice, rubber, plastic, bone.
  --              3d: has a definite mesh. does not flow. surface is fixed.
  --              physics: transmits normal-force. has coefficient-of-restitution.
  --
  --   liquid   — takes the shape of its container. flows. has a free surface.
  --              examples: water, oil, mercury, molten metal, blood.
  --              3d: simulated via fluid shader, surface normal changes dynamically.
  --                  has transparency and refraction (roughness≈0 for clear liquids).
  --              physics: governed by navier-stokes. has viscosity, pressure, density.
  --
  --   gas      — fills its container. invisible or nearly so. diffuses freely.
  --              examples: air, steam, smoke, hydrogen.
  --              3d: rendered as volume (participating medium), smoke shader, alpha.
  --              physics: pressure-based. no fixed surface. compressible.
  --
  -- the default condition for all common-sense material nodes:
  -- room temperature ≈ 20°C (293K), normal pressure ≈ 1 atm.
  -- phase-change-boil and phase-change-freeze handle the transitions.
  --
  -- the apeksha matters: water at 20°C is liquid; at -10°C is solid; at 110°C is gas.
  -- common-sense nodes declare the default phase. the pipeline uses temperature
  -- context to select the correct phase when explicitly stated.

  "common-sense-varga-vishesa"
  "materials-varga-vishesa"

  -- bridges to physics
  "thermodynamics-yukta"          -- phase-change-boil, phase-change-freeze
  "temperature-yukta"             -- default condition: room temperature

  -- bridges to 3d / pratibimba
  "domain-3d-yukta"               -- phase determines render strategy
  "mesh-yukta"                    -- solid: fixed mesh
  "material-yukta"                -- liquid/gas: dynamic shader

  shabda phase, state-of-matter / solid-liquid-or-gas-the-everyday-observable-form-of-a-material-at-room-temperature

